            "kind": "NO_CODE_CHANGE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "yaml/com/ibm/Dump/Create.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 36,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jayanth Othayoth",
                        "email": "ojayanth@gmail.com",
                        "username": "ojayanth"
                    },
                    "message": "NIT: \nThe current design puts all dump-specific parameters into a single\n`CreateParameters` enum. As a result, the interface does not clearly express\nwhich parameters are applicable to which dump types.\n\nFor example, it is not obvious from the interface definition whether:\n\n- `SBEDumpType` is only valid when `DumpType=SBE`\n- `VSPString` is only applicable to `Resource` dumps\n- `FailingUnitId` is only applicable to ?? dumps\n\nThese relationships currently exist only in the implementation and are not\nvisible in the interface definition.\n\nWould it make sense to organize parameters by dump category instead of placing\nall of them under `CreateParameters`?\n\nFor example:\n\n- Top-level/common parameters\n\n  - CreateParameters\n    - DumpType\n    - ErrorLogId\n    - DumpFilesPath\n\n- SBE-specific parameters\n\n  - SBEDumpParameters\n    - TriggerType\n\n  - SBEDumpTriggerType\n    - Timeout\n    - BootFailure\n    - Downstream\n\nThis would make parameter ownership and applicability more obvious and make the\ninterface easier to extend in the future.\n\nExample:\n\n{\n  \"com.ibm.Dump.Create.CreateParameters.DumpType\":\n      \"com.ibm.Dump.Create.DumpType.SBE\",\n\n  \"com.ibm.Dump.Create.SBEDumpParameters.TriggerType\":\n      \"com.ibm.Dump.Create.SBEDumpTriggerType.Timeout\"\n}\n\nThis makes the relationship between `DumpType=SBE` and its associated\nparameters explicit in the interface rather than relying on implementation\ndetails.\nOrganizing parameters by dump category improves clarity, simplifies future extensions, and makes it easier to reuse or standardize common enums and parameter groups across OEMs."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/com/ibm/Dump/Create.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 36,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gopichand Paturi",
                        "email": "gopichandpaturi@gmail.com",
                        "username": "gcpin"
                    },
                    "message": "the current CreateParameters enum is shared across IBM dump creation parameters, so the interface does not strongly express which parameters apply to each dump type.\nFor this patch, I was trying to follow the existing CreateDump\u00a0 documentation, where AdditionalData keys are expected to use the *.Dump.Create.CreateParameters.* enum-string format. \n\nMoving SBE-specific parameters under a separate SBEDumpParameters enum would be a larger interface redesign and may require updates to the base dump-create documentation and existing consumers.\nI have improved the clarity in this patch by documenting the applicability explicitly to clear any ambiguity, for example:\n\nSBEDumpTriggerType: valid only when DumpType is SBE\nDumpFilesPath: path to the collected dump files, currently used by SBE dump creation\nIf we want to reorganize dump parameters by category, I think that should be handled as a separate cleanup/design change so we can update the common interface documentaion and existing callers consistently."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/com/ibm/Dump/Create.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 36,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gopichand Paturi",
                        "email": "gopichandpaturi@gmail.com",
                        "username": "gcpin"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                }
            ],
